            "review_title": "Review at Banh Mi by Minh Nhat",
            "review_text": "Meow\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam95 contributions\n0\nWill not return\nOct 2018 • Couples\nBeing a Saigonese, I guess I’m spoiled by the banh mi culture in SG.\n\nIt was hard to find banh mi stalls in Ha Noi, so we decided to pop our heads in to Minh Nhat for some sandwiches and iced coffees to go.\nWell, staff informed they ran out of eggs, then take-away coffee cups as well, at 10AM on a Sunday.\nThere were only 3 customers (including us), but my own banh mi took 10 minutes to be prepared. \nFlavours were stodgy, and the sandwich came out PRESSED completely flat in a sandwich maker (?)! How very bizarre, and a complete sacrilege. It was also expensive.\n\nBanh mi is supposed to be a super fast, simple, filling and hearty streetfood. The Masterchef-winning-owner marketing for such a dish makes this shop incredibly pretentious.\nRead more\nWritten October 23, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
